==Special Moves==

==== Justice Hurricane ====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=tizoc_6248A, tizoc_6248C, tizoc_6248AC
|input=6248A/C/AC
|input2=360A/C/AC
|description3=Tizoc has a lot of grabs, but this is THE grab. For all of his shortcomings as a character, this is a grab that allows him to cash out for big damage on offense while also being a stellar defensive tool when used as a guard cancel. The exact requirement for the 360 input is as follows:

* At least 3 consecutive cardinal (straight up, down, left or right) directions must be hit. If this requirement is met, the fourth one can be substituted with a diagonal input (for example, 4269 is valid)
* The direction of rotation does not matter. Additionally, diagonal inputs are not necessary for the input (but their inclusion will not invalidate the input sequence). For example, 4268 is valid, but 4862 is also valid.
* The starting point can be any of the four cardinal directions. For example, 2684, 6842, 8426 and 4268 are all valid inputs.

Keep these input requirements in mind, as multiple different versions of the 360 input may be more comfortable for different situations (buffering during a dash, guard cancels, buffering at the end of a jump, etc.)

Additionally, this grab can cancel the first 5 frames of Tizoc's jump, even if that jump is done during the early frames of a dash. This can be used to artificially extend the range of this grab.
----
Light version : 
* Tied with EX/REV for longest range version
* Slowest at 7F, which can actually be advantageous when using as a guard cancel vs deep jump attacks.
* After the animation, immediately press 214AC (brake) to move up to approximately hop distance away from the opponent at +10.
* Tizoc will be much closer to the opponent after the animation if he is backed up to the corner when using this

----
Heavy version :
* More damage and faster startup than the light grab, but shorter range
* Great for guard cancels due to its high damage and extremely fast startup at no additional REV gauge cost. This grab is fast enough to even beat some light chains if used as a guard cancel, assuming the opponent is close enough to get grabbed.
* Leaves Tizoc a little closer to the opponent after the animation compared to the light version. 214AC (brake) will leave you at point-blank range at +6.
* When used while backed up against the corner, one dash leaves Tizoc at point-blank range at +19.

----
REV version :
* Spend some Rev meter to get the range of the light version and the speed of the heavy version in one package, plus massively increased damage (nearly as much as his super grab).
** Rev Accel into 214BD to inflict a total of 377 damage and stay at point-blank range from the opponent with +44 advantage
* Dash twice immediately after the animation ends to be +11 at point blank range, setting up a meaty Close D that will be +5 on block and +9 on hit (enough to link into Close C) without canceling into feint (and feinting will not improve this)
* If used while backed up to the corner, '''360C > hop > feint''' leaves Tizoc at +1 and just close enough to hit 236P or 360A / 360AC, or press 214A (do not brake) to be +11 at point-blank range, similar to the midscreen setup
}}

==== Poseidon Wave ====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=tizoc_214A, tizoc_214C, tizoc_214AC
|input=214A/C/AC
|input2=qcb+A/C/AC
|description3= A running lariat. Unusually nuanced in braking options, and therefore quite useful in many oki setups for its fast forward movement. Launches on counterhit.


----
Light version :
* Used for meterless light confirms. Any special-cancelable attack will combo into this.
* The chest has a hitbox during the slide, but this is -6 on block at best and -9 at worst, making it unsafe. If the hand hitbox is blocked, it is safe at -2.
* Can be braked during the travel to slide Tizoc forward by about half-screen distance without attacking the opponent
----
Heavy version :
* Used to approach the opponent with +2 advantage on block at minimum
* Tizoc backsteps before performing his lariat, making this significantly slower than the other versions.
* Can be braked during the backstep to cancel the lariat entirely, but can also be braked during the travel to slide forward by about half to fullscreen distance, depending on brake timing.
----
EX/REV version :
* This is the go-to move to cancel into from heavies.
* Slides the furthest (nearly fullscreen distance) and recovers fastest when braked, making this a useful (and costly) tool for oki setups.
* Similar on-block situation to the light version, but can be canceled into Rev Blow if Tizoc is in SPG, making this safe on block unless the opponent Guard Cancels into a grab or parry when the 214AC is blocked. Guard Canceled Rev Blows with 22F or faster startup will lose against Tizoc's Rev Blow, and the opponent does not exit blockstun after 214AC in time to counter Tizoc's Rev Blow.
}}

==== Olympus Over ====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=tizoc_214B, tizoc_214D, tizoc_214BD
